    "body": "[Description as provided to ISTS](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1msKBjMAa3mGdDMTFvdkwZ8INz4Tf8kR9fURIUZEtZVI/edit#) below:\n\nDocument scanning\nHow do we stop malicious files from getting to our clients? Integration with CCCS’ assembly line is awesome, but what information is shared with CCCS and would it be a (unreasonable) breach of privacy? Need to work through these questions.\n\n### Acceptance criteria:\n- [x] Review the privacy implications of integrating with CCCS' assembly line for document scanning\n- [x] Conduct an options analysis for file scanning\n- [x] Policy provides a joint recommendation with ISTS on document scanning approach that meets privacy and security requirements (as defined by each group)\n- [x] Document decision in a design document\n",
